RISC3D for RISC OS on Linux (prototype): Linux's side
=======================================================

What it puts where:
  /opt/riscos/rol-3d                        Linux's side: draws for RISC OS
                                            programs with Linux's Mesa (the
                                            GPU's driver: v3d on a Pi 4/5)
  /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian-backports.sources, and
  /etc/apt/preferences.d/riscos-risc3d-mesa    Mesa from trixie-backports

RISC OS's side is the PackMan package RISC3D: !RISC3D in !Boot.Resources
(the RISC3D module, and Linux3D in its GPU folder). riscos-harddisc
installs it; PackMan updates it, as on native RISC OS. Linux3D starts only
where this package is installed.

init (riscos-support 1.0.0049-1 or later) starts rol-3d at start-up. Its
log: /riscos/3d/log.txt.

Programs use it through riscos-mesa's EGL. Set RISC3D$Disable to turn it
off for programs started after.

Zero-copy frames (straight onto the screen) need rol-fb's overlays
(riscos-support 1.0.0048-1 or later) and a 16 million colour mode.

RISC3D's SWI chunk (&5AF80) and error blocks are allocated.
